From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Martins <eduardo@martins.ws>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:16:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: clock: apple,t8010-touch-clock: Add T8015

The A11 PMGR has the touch clock block at offset 0x78000 as well: iBoot
leaves it at 0x800002ee (disabled, divider 750), and the iPhone X ADT's
TCLK(8, 100, 24000000) runs it from the 24 MHz reference.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/clock/apple,t8010-touch-clock.yaml | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/apple,t8010-touch-clock.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/apple,t8010-touch-clock.yaml
index a558d5bd6..f49ce6014 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/apple,t8010-touch-clock.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/apple,t8010-touch-clock.yaml
@@ -13,7 +13,8 @@ description:
   The T7000 and T8010 PMGR contain a gate and integer divider for the
   reference clock consumed by the touchscreen controller. The S8000 PMGR has
   the same block at the same offset; the iPad 5 N1 touchscreen runs it at
-  32768 Hz.
+  32768 Hz. So has the T8015 PMGR, whose iPhone X touchscreen runs it at
+  24 MHz.
 
 properties:
   compatible:
@@ -22,7 +23,9 @@ properties:
           - apple,t7000-touch-clock
           - apple,t8010-touch-clock
       - items:
-          - const: apple,s8000-touch-clock
+          - enum:
+              - apple,s8000-touch-clock
+              - apple,t8015-touch-clock
           - const: apple,t8010-touch-clock
 
   reg:
